For the defining doublet of $SU(2)$, $\mathbf2\otimes\mathbf2=\mathbf3_S\oplus\mathbf1_A.$ Writing the two basis states as $u$ and $d$, the symmetric triplet is $\begin{aligned}
\ket{1,1}&=\ket{uu},\\
\ket{1,0}&=\frac{1}{\sqrt2}\bigl(\ket{ud}+\ket{du}\bigr),\\
\ket{1,-1}&=\ket{dd},\end{aligned}$ while the antisymmetric singlet is $\ket{0,0}
=\frac{1}{\sqrt2}\bigl(\ket{ud}-\ket{du}\bigr).$ This is the familiar addition of two spin-$\tfrac12$ angular momenta: the four raw states reorganize into spin one and spin zero.

