p.src:
Electric charge is a linear combination of generators. On the matter column in Eq. , it acts as $Q_{\overline5}
=
\operatorname{diag}
\left(0,-1,\frac13,\frac13,\frac13\right),
\qquad
\operatorname{tr}Q_{\overline5}=0.$ Thus $0-1+3\left(\frac13\right)=0.$ Replacing the anti-down fields by down fields would instead give $0-1+3\left(-\frac13\right)=-2,$ which cannot be the trace of an $SU(5)$ generator. The apparently strange anti-down assignment is therefore forced by the group structure.

