p.src:
The matter multiplets can be unified still further. Under $SO(10)\supset SU(5),$ one spinor representation decomposes as $\mathbf{16}
\longrightarrow
\mathbf{10}\oplus\overline{\mathbf5}\oplus\mathbf1.$ The singlet is naturally identified with a left-handed antineutrino, or equivalently the charge conjugate of a right-handed neutrino. Thus all sixteen fields of an extended family fit into one irreducible $SO(10)$ multiplet.

